  "data": {
   "answer": "France's stock coverage in June 2026 is about 8.7 months. On that basis, the stock runs out around March 2027. The figure compares stock at standard cost (about €28.4M) with the next 24 months of forecast cost of goods sold (about €77.1M).\n\nI used the value basis (EUR) because the usual kg/L-equivalent basis was refused. France's items mix kg and L, so those units can't be added together.\n\nTwo warnings came back:\n- **FORECAST_GAPS_FILLED (20):** 20 item-months in the forecast horizon had no forecast row, so they were counted as zero demand.\n- **DEFAULT_SCOPE_EXCLUDED:** About €15.45M of BULK stock was left out because it has no forecast. Including it would require filtering item type explicitly.\n\nData freshness: 2026-06-01",
